# Arguments for llama-server, consumed by llama-server.service.
# Single logical line, word-split by systemd. Restart after editing:
#   systemctl --user restart llama-server.service
#
# Bound to 127.0.0.1 on purpose: llama-server has no authentication.
# Model weights are cached under ~/.cache/llama.cpp (LLAMA_CACHE in the unit).
# --jinja is required for OpenAI-style tool calling; without it the server
# returns 500 on any request carrying a tools parameter.
#
# Qwen3-Coder-Next: 80B total / 3B active, ~49.6 GB at UD-Q4_K_XL. Requires the
# 64 GiB GTT pool (amdgpu.gttsize / ttm.pages_limit kargs) -- it does not fit in
# the kernel default of half of RAM. Measured on a HX 370 / 890M via Vulkan at
# 49/49 layers offloaded: ~57 t/s prompt, ~15 t/s generation at 4K context.
#
# Long context on gfx1150 is not fully proven: llama.cpp #24861 reports a
# CPU-side Vulkan hang between 8K and 16K depth on this chip (seen with other
# models). If generation stalls at depth, drop -c and retest before assuming a
# model problem.
LLAMA_SERVER_ARGS=-hf unsloth/Qwen3-Coder-Next-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL --alias qwen3-coder-next --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080 -ngl 99 -c 65536 -fa on --jinja --temp 0.7 --top-p 0.8 --top-k 20 --repeat-penalty 1.05
